  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "R11-formal-parity-fidelity",
      "reason": "The source, freshly exported declarations, contract and supplied blind readback agree on the real scalar domain and every quantified hypothesis. For arbitrary natural n, including zero, PairIndex is Fin n ⊕ Fin n; reversal swaps tags at the same index. Its second half therefore uses mirrored-pair order. T=[[I,I],[I,-I]] and S=T/2 are mutually inverse, and K=SJT is a similarity. The relation JP=aPJ is explicitly assumed for arbitrary real a. Anticommutation forces K11=K22=0; commutation forces K12=K21=0. Determinant invariance and det([[0,C],[D,0]])=(-1)^n det(C)det(D) require no invertibility and include empty matrices. For every real vector pair x,v, the affine increment is -Pv; preserving increments correspond to Pv=-v and reversing increments to Pv=v, with both conditions holding at v=0. The root retains all these hypotheses. No permutation to physically increasing indices, differential Jacobian identification, or concrete program correctness is established.",
      "verdict": "APPROVED"
    },
    {
      "id": "R11-formal-boundary-fidelity",
      "reason": "All explicit matrix entries match the contract, blind readback and the relevant submitted formula. Direct algebra gives det(Me)=L(L+2)[L(L+1)-(L-1)(L-2)]=2L(L+2)(2L-1) and det(Mo)=L(L+2)[L(L+3)-(L+1)(L-2)]=2L(L+2)(2L+1), for every real L. Positivity is restricted to real L≥4. At L=4 the determinants are 336 and 432; at L=0 both vanish, consistently with the stated scope. For every natural L≥4, the real block-diagonal matrix has positive determinant, hence its multiplication map is bijective: every real residual vector has exactly one real coefficient vector. Evenness is not required by this algebraic theorem. Polynomial trace derivation, parity-sector residual conversion, complex extension, continuity and approximation are explicitly outside the formal target.",
      "verdict": "APPROVED"
    },
